      ],
      "chunk_id": "83a57bc9-ac5f-411e-9684-7d80d72edf1f",
      "content": "Policy Status\n\nThis policy is effective February 1, 2026 and replaces the 2025 informal spend guidance. If an older team wiki or email thread lists a different limit, this policy controls unless Finance publishes a newer version.\n\nEmployees should submit expenses within 30 calendar days of the transaction date. Expenses submitted after 60 calendar days require manager approval and a Finance Operations exception note.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002007",
      "document_id": "FIN-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "08133959-8b36-4832-8e3a-9c76796459f3",
      "content": "Reimbursement Timing\n\nApproved expense reports are reimbursed in the next regular payroll cycle when submitted at least five business days before payroll close. Reports submitted after the cutoff move to the following payroll cycle.\n\nFinance may hold reimbursement if the report lacks required receipts, approval, business purpose, or attendee information. The hold is administrative and does not imply misconduct.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002007",
      "document_id": "FIN-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "22e6e0ed-a681-4701-97d1-c1be7d69b0c0",
      "content": "Expense Categories\n\n| Category | Standard Limit | Approval Required |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Meals during business travel | USD 85 per day | Manager approval above limit |\n| Customer-facing meals | USD 125 per attendee | Manager approval and attendee list |\n| Office supplies | USD 300 per purchase | Manager approval above limit |\n| Software subscription trial | USD 500 annualized value | IT review and manager approval |\n| Conference registration | USD 1,500 per event | Manager approval before purchase |\n\nAlcohol is not reimbursable unless it is part of a customer-facing meal approved by a manager before the event. Gift cards, personal devices, fines, commuting costs, and family travel are not reimbursable.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002007",
      "document_id": "FIN-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "2f70e93f-c560-4b48-8a79-caa4306033ef",
      "content": "Exceptions\n\nEmergency expenses are allowed when waiting for approval would create a customer, employee safety, or business-continuity risk. The employee must document the emergency and obtain manager approval within three business days.\n\nRecurring exceptions must be converted into a purchase order or department budget request. Finance does not approve repeated one-off exceptions for predictable monthly costs.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002007",
      "document_id": "FIN-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "a0d5c223-14ab-407a-a287-0d893981a570",
      "content": "Receipt Requirements\n\nReceipts are required for every expense above USD 25. A credit card statement is not enough by itself when the merchant receipt is available. Missing receipts require a signed missing-receipt attestation that explains the business purpose, amount, date, and merchant.\n\nExpense reports must include the business purpose in plain language. A report labeled only \"meeting,\" \"travel,\" or \"miscellaneous\" will be returned for correction.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002007",
      "document_id": "FIN-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    }
  ],
